      },
      "text": "## Layer 1: The Epipolar Constraint — Search Becomes 1D"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md#006",
      "path": [
        "06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:computer-vision:06-multiview-geometry, git-history:computer-vision:06-multiview-geometry]",
        "canonical_path": "computer-vision/06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md",
        "concepts": "[epipolar geometry, fundamental matrix, essential matrix, stereo, triangulation, RANSAC, homography]",
        "current_path": "computer-vision/06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md",
        "id": "maxim:computer-vision:multiview-geometry",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "computer-vision",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[multi-view geometry]",
        "section": "computing-software",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Multi-View Geometry",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Given a point `x1` in image 1, where is its match in image 2? Without geometry you would\nsearch the whole image (2D). The epipolar constraint reduces this to a *single line* —\nthe **epipolar line** — because the true match must lie on the projection of the ray\nthrough `x1`."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md#007",
      "path": [
        "06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:computer-vision:06-multiview-geometry, git-history:computer-vision:06-multiview-geometry]",
        "canonical_path": "computer-vision/06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md",
        "concepts": "[epipolar geometry, fundamental matrix, essential matrix, stereo, triangulation, RANSAC, homography]",
        "current_path": "computer-vision/06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md",
        "id": "maxim:computer-vision:multiview-geometry",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "computer-vision",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[multi-view geometry]",
        "section": "computing-software",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Multi-View Geometry",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                        EPIPOLAR GEOMETRY                                     |\n|                                                                              |\n|                            X (somewhere on this ray)                         |\n|                           /:\\                                                |\n|                          / : \\                                               |\n|                         /  :  \\                                              |\n|              image1    /   :   \\    image2                                   |\n|             +--------+/    :    \\+--------+                                  |\n|             |   x1 . |     :     | . . . .|  <- epipolar LINE l2:            |\n|             |        |     :     |  the image of x1's ray                    |\n|             |  e1 .  |     :     |  . e2  |  <- epipoles e1,e2 = image of    |\n|             +--------+     :     +--------+     the OTHER camera center      |\n|                  C1 -------:------- C2                                       |\n|                       baseline                                               |\n|                                                                              |\n|   The two image planes, the two centers, and X all lie in ONE epipolar       |\n|   plane. Its intersection with each image is an epipolar line.               |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md#008",
      "path": [
        "06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:computer-vision:06-multiview-geometry, git-history:computer-vision:06-multiview-geometry]",
        "canonical_path": "computer-vision/06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md",
        "concepts": "[epipolar geometry, fundamental matrix, essential matrix, stereo, triangulation, RANSAC, homography]",
        "current_path": "computer-vision/06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md",
        "id": "maxim:computer-vision:multiview-geometry",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "computer-vision",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[multi-view geometry]",
        "section": "computing-software",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Multi-View Geometry",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "| Term | Definition |\n|------|------------|\n| **Epipolar plane** | Plane through `X`, `C1`, `C2` |\n| **Epipolar line** | Intersection of the epipolar plane with an image |\n| **Epipole** | Image of one camera's center in the other view; all epipolar lines pass through it |\n| **Baseline** | The line `C1`–`C2` joining the two centers |"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md#009",
      "path": [
        "06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:computer-vision:06-multiview-geometry, git-history:computer-vision:06-multiview-geometry]",
        "canonical_path": "computer-vision/06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md",
        "concepts": "[epipolar geometry, fundamental matrix, essential matrix, stereo, triangulation, RANSAC, homography]",
        "current_path": "computer-vision/06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md",
        "id": "maxim:computer-vision:multiview-geometry",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "computer-vision",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[multi-view geometry]",
        "section": "computing-software",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Multi-View Geometry",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The payoff: stereo matching searches a 1D line, not a 2D plane — a quadratic-to-linear\nreduction in the matching problem."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md#010",
      "path": [
