      "text": "## Layer 2: The Fundamental Matrix F"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md#012",
      "path": [
        "06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:computer-vision:06-multiview-geometry, git-history:computer-vision:06-multiview-geometry]",
        "canonical_path": "computer-vision/06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md",
        "concepts": "[epipolar geometry, fundamental matrix, essential matrix, stereo, triangulation, RANSAC, homography]",
        "current_path": "computer-vision/06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md",
        "id": "maxim:computer-vision:multiview-geometry",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "computer-vision",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[multi-view geometry]",
        "section": "computing-software",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Multi-View Geometry",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The epipolar constraint is captured algebraically by the **fundamental matrix** `F`, a\n3x3 rank-2 matrix relating corresponding *pixel* coordinates in two **uncalibrated**\nviews."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md#013",
      "path": [
        "06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:computer-vision:06-multiview-geometry, git-history:computer-vision:06-multiview-geometry]",
        "canonical_path": "computer-vision/06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md",
        "concepts": "[epipolar geometry, fundamental matrix, essential matrix, stereo, triangulation, RANSAC, homography]",
        "current_path": "computer-vision/06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md",
        "id": "maxim:computer-vision:multiview-geometry",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "computer-vision",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[multi-view geometry]",
        "section": "computing-software",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Multi-View Geometry",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n   For corresponding points x1, x2 (homogeneous pixel coords):"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md#014",
      "path": [
        "06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:computer-vision:06-multiview-geometry, git-history:computer-vision:06-multiview-geometry]",
        "canonical_path": "computer-vision/06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md",
        "concepts": "[epipolar geometry, fundamental matrix, essential matrix, stereo, triangulation, RANSAC, homography]",
        "current_path": "computer-vision/06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md",
        "id": "maxim:computer-vision:multiview-geometry",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "computer-vision",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[multi-view geometry]",
        "section": "computing-software",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Multi-View Geometry",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "x2^T F x1 = 0          <- THE epipolar constraint"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md#015",
      "path": [
        "06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:computer-vision:06-multiview-geometry, git-history:computer-vision:06-multiview-geometry]",
        "canonical_path": "computer-vision/06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md",
        "concepts": "[epipolar geometry, fundamental matrix, essential matrix, stereo, triangulation, RANSAC, homography]",
        "current_path": "computer-vision/06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md",
        "id": "maxim:computer-vision:multiview-geometry",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "computer-vision",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[multi-view geometry]",
        "section": "computing-software",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Multi-View Geometry",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Meaning: F x1 = l2 is the epipolar LINE in image 2 on which x2 must lie.\n            F^T x2 = l1 is the epipolar line in image 1."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md#016",
      "path": [
        "06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:computer-vision:06-multiview-geometry, git-history:computer-vision:06-multiview-geometry]",
        "canonical_path": "computer-vision/06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md",
        "concepts": "[epipolar geometry, fundamental matrix, essential matrix, stereo, triangulation, RANSAC, homography]",
        "current_path": "computer-vision/06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md",
        "id": "maxim:computer-vision:multiview-geometry",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
