        "title": "Multi-View Geometry",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "`F` is estimated from point correspondences. Each match `x2^T F x1 = 0` gives one linear\nequation in the 9 entries of `F`; eight matches determine it (up to scale)."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md#019",
      "path": [
        "06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:computer-vision:06-multiview-geometry, git-history:computer-vision:06-multiview-geometry]",
        "canonical_path": "computer-vision/06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md",
        "concepts": "[epipolar geometry, fundamental matrix, essential matrix, stereo, triangulation, RANSAC, homography]",
        "current_path": "computer-vision/06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md",
        "id": "maxim:computer-vision:multiview-geometry",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "computer-vision",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[multi-view geometry]",
        "section": "computing-software",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Multi-View Geometry",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                  NORMALIZED 8-POINT ALGORITHM (estimate F)                   |\n|                                                                              |\n|  1. NORMALIZE   translate/scale points so they are centered, ~unit spread    |\n|                 (Hartley normalization -- essential for numerical stability) |\n|  2. BUILD A     each match -> one row of A from x2^T F x1 = 0; stack >= 8    |\n|  3. SVD of A    F = the singular vector for the smallest singular value      |\n|                 (least-squares null space)                                   |\n|  4. ENFORCE     SVD F = U S V^T; zero the smallest singular value; recompose |\n|     RANK 2      -> guarantees det F = 0 (valid epipolar geometry)            |\n|  5. DENORMALIZE undo the step-1 transform                                    |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md#020",
      "path": [
        "06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:computer-vision:06-multiview-geometry, git-history:computer-vision:06-multiview-geometry]",
        "canonical_path": "computer-vision/06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md",
        "concepts": "[epipolar geometry, fundamental matrix, essential matrix, stereo, triangulation, RANSAC, homography]",
        "current_path": "computer-vision/06-MULTIVIEW-GEOMETRY.md",
        "id": "maxim:computer-vision:multiview-geometry",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "computer-vision",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[multi-view geometry]",
        "section": "computing-software",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Multi-View Geometry",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Bridge — linear algebra:** every step is SVD. Solving `A f = 0` for the homogeneous\nnull space is \"smallest-singular-vector of `A`\"; enforcing rank 2 is \"zero the smallest\nsingular value of `F`.\" Hartley's normalization is the difference between a usable `F`\nand numerical garbage."
    },
